Ready for your next career move? KLM aims to become the most data- and technology-driven airline in the world – and CHIP is right at the heart of it. As a Business Product Analyst (BPA), you keep the engine room of Schiphol’s ground operations running: the system that plans and allocates people and resources every day across Passenger Services, Baggage Services and Apron Services. You don’t just fix what’s broken – you understand why things work the way they do, and turn that insight into smarter, scalable solutions for the entire operation.

**What will you do?**

As a Business Product Analyst, you help the product team get the most out of our product. That starts in the operation, and we mean that literally: put on your safety shoes and talk to planners, shift leaders and operational staff to understand what’s really going on. With that knowledge, you make sure our IT solution CHIP is configured and maintained according to the right requirements, help implement changes to business processes, and make sure users truly embrace the system.

In practice, you will:

* translate operational processes into CHIP application logic – model new functionality in Perl and make full use of standard functionality before turning to custom solutions;
* configure and optimise resource planning and allocation functionality, business rules, parameters, interfaces and system settings (including BDE and .ini configuration);
* spot improvement opportunities before anyone asks – and reuse solutions across Passenger, Baggage and Aircraft/Apron Services instead of reinventing the wheel every time;
* dig into incidents with SQL, find the root cause (not just the symptom), and work with vendors and developers to fix it for good;
* develop and maintain scripts, queries and automated tests in Perl, Python and SQL;
* coordinate testing, releases, changes and operational handovers, and keep functional and technical documentation sharp and up to date;
* contribute to CHIP’s cloud journey, and take part in the on-call/standby rotation that supports a business-critical 24/7 operation.

**Where do you land?**

You’ll join the CHIP team at Platform Ground, part of Data & Technology – working alongside enthusiastic colleagues in Amsterdam and Budapest. CHIP is indispensable to the handling of Passenger Services, Baggage Services and Apron Services, so your work has a direct, visible impact on day-to-day operations at Schiphol. Our department has an innovative culture: think Hackweek, dedicated time for Learning & Development, and participation in the BPA Community of Practice. We’re building an inclusive atmosphere where you can be yourself – regardless of what you look like, what’s in your passport, how you identify, what you believe, or who you hug when you get home. In short: it’s not about who you are, but how you are.

**Your profile**

**What will you learn?:**

This role doesn’t put you in a box – it’s a springboard. You’ll rotate between Passenger Services, Aircraft Service

